THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
----------------------

NOAH deploys and orchestrates third-party software — among others Garage
(AGPL-3.0), CloudNativePG, Velero, OpenEBS and Harbor (Apache-2.0), and sanoid,
PowerDNS and Forgejo (GPL). Each remains under its own licence, held by its own
authors.

Deploying such software constitutes aggregation, not the creation of a derived
work, and imposes nothing on NOAH itself. Two cases are different and carry
their own obligations:

  - distributing an appliance image that bundles these components, which
    triggers the duty to supply their licences and corresponding sources;
  - modifying Garage as part of a managed offering, where the AGPL network
    clause requires those modifications to be published.


